    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe customerCode format is now `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the sole place `customerCode` is generated:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of `city`\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- `NNNN` = per-city 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the owners already in that city (filtering `findAll()` by `city`, case-insensitively). It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the owner being created is not counted.\n\nExample output: `SYD-SMI-0007`.\n\n**Values derived from customerCode:** The only one is `membershipNumber` (`MembershipNumber.of`, wired in `OwnerMapper`), which formats `<customerCode>-M<YY>`. Because it takes the `customerCode` string verbatim as input, it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`) with no logic change. I updated its javadoc example and the `openapi.yml` descriptions/examples for both `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` to match.\n\nThe schema column `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` comfortably fits the new 12-char format.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes.",
